item.text:
Accepted new evidence follows. I kept the set focused on 2022 conduct plus a small amount of later retrospective context where it helped calibrate the 2022 trajectory. No score.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Executive Order 14066 - Prohibiting Certain Imports and New Investments With Respect to Continued Russian Federation Efforts To Undermine the Sovereignty and Territorial Integrity of Ukraine","publisher":"The American Presidency Project","publication_date":"2022-03-08","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-14066-prohibiting-certain-imports-and-new-investments-with-respect","claim":"Biden expanded the Russian national emergency because Russia's war against Ukraine violated international law and threatened the peace, stability, sovereignty, and territorial integrity of Ukraine.","locator":"lines 64-64","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Presidential order reproduced from the official record with direct attribution and exact date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden as President.","contrary_evidence":["This is coercive statecraft, not a negotiated settlement or peace agreement."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.3","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. Treasury Guidance on President Biden’s Executive Order","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-03-08","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0641","claim":"Treasury said Biden's oil, LNG, and coal ban was meant to deprive Putin of resources for his war of choice.","locator":"line 604","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Treasury guidance on an announced presidential action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden’s sanctions decision.","contrary_evidence":["Sanctions can increase pressure without quickly shortening war or restoring lawful peace."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. Sanctions on Russia: Legal Authorities and Related Actions","publisher":"Congress.gov | Library of Congress","publication_date":"2024-03-28","url":"https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R48052","claim":"CRS summarizes Biden's February to April 2022 executive orders as prohibiting trade and investment in occupied Ukrainian regions, banning Russian energy imports, and restricting additional Russian imports and investment.","locator":"lines 664-671 and 770-771","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Neutral legislative-research summary of the legal authority and 2022 sanction sequence.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly covers the 2022 sanctions sequence, though the product page is later.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Biden’s 2022 Russia policy.","contrary_evidence":["Legal restrictions are punitive pressure, not direct evidence of de-escalation success."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden Signs Order Transferring Arms to Ukrainian Defenders","publisher":"U.S. Department of Defense","publication_date":"2022-03-16","url":"https://www.defense.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/2968823/biden-signs-order-transferring-arms-to-ukrainian-defenders/","claim":"Biden approved an $800 million transfer of weapons and said the U.S. would do everything possible to push for an end to the war while helping Ukraine defend itself.","locator":"lines 243-251 and 285-297","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary contemporaneous DoD account of a presidential security-assistance decision.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's wartime decision-making.","contrary_evidence":["Arming Ukraine can also prolong fighting and carries escalation risk."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine calls for no-fly zone to stop Russian bombardment","publisher":"Reuters via Nippon.com","publication_date":"2022-03-01","url":"https://www.nippon.com/en/news/reu20220228KBN2KX0AS/","claim":"The United States ruled out sending troops or enforcing a no-fly zone because that would risk direct conflict and war with Russia.","locator":"lines 25-28","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on an explicit White House de-escalation choice, hosted by Nippon.com.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 invasion crisis.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's restraint choices through White House policy.","contrary_evidence":["Refusing a no-fly zone reduced escalation but left Ukraine exposed to Russian attack."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"‘Armageddon’ warning reflects Biden’s instincts about Putin","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/07/biden-putin-nuclear-armageddon/","claim":"The Post reported that Biden's Armageddon warning was not based on new intelligence and that U.S. officials were already in back-channel communication with Russia about the consequences of nuclear use.","locator":"lines 30-34 and 55-59","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting with direct quotes from officials and the White House context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's public crisis messaging and the administration's response.","contrary_evidence":["Several officials and allies thought the rhetoric was unusually stark and potentially provocative."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"No new intelligence behind Biden Armageddon comment - White House","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/politics/white-house-after-bidens-comments-says-still-no-need-for-us-to-change-nuclear-posture-2907545","claim":"Reuters reported that the White House said it had no new intelligence and saw no reason to change nuclear posture after Biden's Armageddon remark.","locator":"lines 407-420","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters contemporaneous report with direct White House attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's public warning and the administration's clarification.","contrary_evidence":["The comment itself was more alarming than the policy state the White House described."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Speech | NATO Transcript","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2022-06-27","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/events/transcripts/2022/06/27/speech","claim":"At Madrid, NATO leaders said Russia's invasion had shattered peace in Europe and justified a new security posture.","locator":"lines 789-796","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official summit transcript from the alliance central to U.S. security policy.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong, as Biden chaired the U.S. role in the summit and alliance line.","contrary_evidence":["Alliance deterrence strengthens security but also hardens bloc confrontation."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pre-Summit press conference","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2022-06-27","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/events/transcripts/2022/06/27/pre-summit-press-conference","claim":"NATO said Russia was the most significant and direct threat and that the summit would strengthen forward defenses and address cyber and hybrid threats.","locator":"lines 826-834","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official NATO transcript describing the 2022 strategic response landscape.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Biden's alliance management.","contrary_evidence":["Strengthening defenses is compatible with restraint, but not itself a peace settlement."],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Factbox-U.N.-led deal to ensure safe export of Ukraine's grain","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-07-23","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/07/23/us-ukraine-crisis-grains-turkey-factbox","claim":"The Black Sea grain deal created a monitored de facto ceasefire for covered ports and was designed to avert famine by restoring Ukrainian food exports.","locator":"lines 670-688 and 696-701","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters factbox summarizing a U.N.-brokered agreement with specific implementation details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant, since the United States publicly backed the deal and linked it to Ukraine policy.","contrary_evidence":["The deal was necessary because Russia had blocked exports; it did not end the war."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Report on the Human Rights situation in Ukraine","publisher":"United Nations in Ukraine / OHCHR","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://ukraine.un.org/en/201055-report-human-rights-situation-ukraine","claim":"OHCHR verified 12,649 civilian casualties in Ukraine in the reporting period and said the actual number was likely higher.","locator":"lines 69-69","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN human-rights monitoring report with verified casualty totals.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly covers the 2022 war environment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Biden's support, restraint, and accountability choices.","contrary_evidence":["The casualties are caused by the war itself, not by Biden personally."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine: Amid mounting human cost, parties must uphold international humanitarian law","publisher":"ICRC","publication_date":"2022-03-04","url":"https://www.icrc.org/en/document/ukraine-amid-mounting-human-cost-parties-must-uphold-international-humanitarian-law-0","claim":"ICRC reminded the parties in Ukraine to spare the civilian population from military operations and allow safe passage for people fleeing the fighting.","locator":"line 191","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative humanitarian-law reminder from the neutral ICRC.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 conflict period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for assessing Biden's military and diplomatic choices.","contrary_evidence":["This is a general law-of-war reminder, not a U.S.-specific finding."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine: Like A Prison Convoy: Russia's Unlawful Transfer And Abuse of Civilians In Ukraine During 'Filtration'","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-11-10","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/eur50/6136/2022/en/","claim":"Amnesty said Russian and Russian-controlled forces committed war crimes and likely crimes against humanity by unlawfully transferring or deporting civilians and abusing them in filtration processes.","locator":"line 68","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed field report based on on-the-ground investigation and document review.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 war period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Biden's support to Ukraine and accountability posture.","contrary_evidence":["This documents Russian conduct, not a Biden action."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine: Humanitarian Catastrophe in Izium. The Plight of Civilians under Bombardment and Siege-like Conditions","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/eur50/5382/2022/en/","claim":"Amnesty described Izium as being on the edge of a humanitarian catastrophe under bombardment and siege-like conditions after Russia's invasion.","locator":"lines 67-68","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights reporting focused on civilian suffering in the war zone.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Biden's crisis response and support to Ukraine.","contrary_evidence":["This is civilian-harm context, not a direct evaluation of Biden's own conduct."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine: Ukrainian fighting tactics endanger civilians","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-08-04","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/08/ukraine-ukrainian-fighting-tactics-endanger-civilians/","claim":"Amnesty said Ukrainian forces put civilians at risk by operating weapons systems in populated residential areas, even while stressing that this did not justify Russian attacks.","locator":"lines 67-76","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent but controversial rights report, useful as contrary evidence on proxy conduct and civilian risk.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context; relevant because U.S. support did not fully control Ukrainian battlefield conduct.","contrary_evidence":["The report was heavily criticized and concerns Ukrainian conduct do not translate into a Biden-directed policy failure."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.5","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden makes surprise visit to Kyiv","publisher":"Associated Press","publication_date":"2023-02-20","url":"https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-biden-kyiv-politics-74c9de636c489393c86ad115e5cbcb48","claim":"AP reported that Biden's 2023 Kyiv trip was pre-notified to Moscow for deconfliction to avoid miscalculation between two nuclear-armed states.","locator":"lines 2311-2314","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous AP reporting on a directly relevant later crisis-management decision.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Later retrospective on the 2022-2023 Ukraine-war trajectory.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's crisis-management style.","contrary_evidence":["This is later than the target year and does not itself prove 2022 conduct."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden unveils new Ukraine weapons package, Russia sanctions","publisher":"Associated Press","publication_date":"2023-02-24","url":"https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-us-department-of-the-treasury-government-janet-yellen-business-f85483ad976990a056c9bfc6b504a07d","claim":"On the first anniversary of the invasion, the administration announced new sanctions and a $2 billion weapons package and ruled out F-16s for the near term.","locator":"lines 1809-1811","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"AP report with clear attribution and concrete policy details.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Later retrospective on Biden's wartime policy trajectory.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's continued Ukraine policy.","contrary_evidence":["This is a later follow-on, not a 2022 event, and sanctions do not end war by themselves."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine uses long-range missiles provided by US for first time","publisher":"Associated Press","publication_date":"2024-05-04","url":"https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-war-long-range-missiles-4d2254639eb5a503d8b0a291ed0680e9","claim":"AP reported that Biden approved delivery of ATACMS in February and that the March package included a significant number of them after an escalation review.","locator":"lines 1948-1950","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"AP later reporting on a Biden-era escalation-management decision with specific attribution.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Later retrospective on Biden's escalation-management choices.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden, though later than the target year.","contrary_evidence":["This is later than 2022 and reflects a continued balancing of military aid and escalation risk."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.5","2B.8"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 52
- Documents opened: 30
- Duplicate or syndicated copies collapsed: 14
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items discarded: 10
- Inaccessible or technical-error items: 8
- Accepted distinct URLs: 18

Material gaps:
- I still do not have a clean 2022 primary transcript for Biden's own public Ukraine speech and NATO alliance statements from White House archives because several archived State/White House pages were technically inaccessible in this environment.
- Direct 2022 evidence on private diplomacy, ceasefire channels, and U.S. restraint rules for partner weapons use is thinner than the public sanctions and aid record.
- Proxy-control and civilian-protection evidence is mostly indirect because Biden did not control Ukrainian battlefield conduct; the useful line is therefore "support plus restraint" rather than direct command responsibility.
- The strongest contrary material is that U.S. aid and sanctions may prolong the war even when they are lawful and defensively framed.

Next best directions:
- Add archived White House or State transcript pages for Biden's March and September 2022 Ukraine remarks if accessible through alternate archives.
- Look for contemporaneous U.S. policy notes on end-use limits, no-strike guidance, and deconfliction channels with Russia.
- Add one or two specialist scholarship pieces on whether the 2022 U.S. approach shortened, prolonged, or stabilized the war, to sharpen 2B.2, 2B.7, and 2B.10.
